From 261238e5743b07a13831400f9c5f1b23e4ad1e0b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Bernal <david.f.bernal@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 01:52:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] libavoid: apply pin connection cost at the target end of a
 connector

AStarPathPrivate::search() gave the final step onto the target's dummy
pin-helper vertex no cost (node.g = bestNode->g). The pin's connection
cost and portDirectionPenalty are stored on exactly that edge (see
ConnEnd::assignPinVisibilityTo), so ShapeConnectionPin::setConnectionCost
only had an effect at the source end of a connector.

Add the edge's cost beyond its geometric length on that step. A* only
terminates when the target is popped, so the cheapest pin now wins, and
the heuristic stays admissible.

Repro: two pins of one class on the target shape, cost 0 on the top
side and 1600 on the left; the router picked the left pin. Reversing
the connector (pins on the source) picked the top pin.

---
 cola/libavoid/makepath.cpp | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/cola/libavoid/makepath.cpp b/cola/libavoid/makepath.cpp
index 713498ec..8050a0b3 100644
--- a/cola/libavoid/makepath.cpp
+++ b/cola/libavoid/makepath.cpp
@@ -1443,8 +1443,14 @@ void AStarPathPrivate::search(ConnRef *lineRef, VertInf *src, VertInf *tar, Vert
                 if (node.inf->id.isDummyPinHelper())
                 {
                     // This is connecting to a connection pin helper vertex.
-                    // There should be no additional cost for this step.
-                    node.g = bestNode->g;
+                    // There is no extra path length for this step, but the
+                    // pin's connection cost (and portDirectionPenalty) live
+                    // on this edge, so add them.  Otherwise pin costs only
+                    // apply at the source end of a connector.
+                    double pinDist = (isOrthogonal) ?
+                            manhattanDist(bestNodeInf->point, node.inf->point) :
+                            euclideanDist(bestNodeInf->point, node.inf->point);
+                    node.g = bestNode->g + std::max(0.0, edgeDist - pinDist);
                 }
                 else
                 {
